== 2.6 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The stores ledger differs from the bin card because the stores ledger],
  [records both quantities and values],
  [is a book of original entry],
  [records quantities only],
  [is kept by the supplier]
)

#mcq(2, [The document that authorises the store to issue material to a department is the],
  [purchase order],
  [goods received note],
  [bin card],
  [stores requisition]
)

#mcq(3, [Stock of 200 units at ₦10 is followed by a receipt of 300 units at ₦12. Under FIFO, the value of an issue of 250 units is],
  [₦2,600],
  [₦3,000],
  [₦2,500],
  [₦2,800]
)

#mcq(4, [Using the same stock, the value of the issue under LIFO is],
  [₦2,500],
  [₦3,000],
  [₦2,600],
  [₦2,800]
)

#mcq(5, [Under the weighted average method, the issue price is],
  [the market price on the issue date],
  [total stock value divided by total units after each receipt],
  [the newest price in stock],
  [the oldest price in stock]
)

#mcq(6, [When prices are rising, LIFO produces],
  [the highest closing stock],
  [a closing stock equal to the average],
  [the lowest closing stock],
  [the same closing stock as FIFO]
)

#mcq(7, [The economic order quantity is the quantity at which],
  [ordering cost equals holding cost],
  [stock is at its maximum],
  [stock reaches the reorder level],
  [the supplier gives the largest discount]
)

#mcq(8, [Maximum usage 500 units a week, maximum lead time 4 weeks. The reorder level is],
  [500 units],
  [2,000 units],
  [2,500 units],
  [1,250 units]
)

#mcq(9, [Reorder level 2,000 units; average usage 400 a week; average lead time 3 weeks. The minimum level is],
  [1,200 units],
  [400 units],
  [2,000 units],
  [800 units]
)

#mcq(10, [A physical stock count shows less stock than the bin card. The difference is],
  [an abnormal gain],
  [a stock loss, written off],
  [added to purchases],
  [ignored until the year end]
)

#mcq(11, [Under the time rate, a worker's wage is],
  [the value of the work certified],
  [a share of the firm's profit],
  [units produced × rate per unit],
  [hours worked × rate per hour]
)

#mcq(12, [Under a piece rate system, the worker is paid according to],
  [units completed],
  [seniority],
  [the department's overhead],
  [hours worked]
)

#mcq(13, [Idle time is the time during which],
  [a machine is fully used],
  [stock is being counted],
  [a worker works overtime],
  [a worker is paid but produces nothing]
)

#mcq(14, [Idle time is normally charged as],
  [factory overhead],
  [administration expense],
  [a deduction from the wage],
  [direct labour]
)

#mcq(15, [A worker is paid ₦400 an hour for a 40-hour week and works 6 hours of overtime at time and a half. His gross wage is],
  [₦19,600],
  [₦16,000],
  [₦18,400],
  [₦17,600]
)

#mcq(16, [The overtime premium is the],
  [basic rate for overtime hours],
  [whole overtime payment],
  [deduction from gross pay],
  [part of the overtime payment above the basic rate]
)

#mcq(17, [An overtime premium caused by a particular urgent order is charged as],
  [administration cost],
  [direct labour of that order],
  [factory overhead],
  [selling cost]
)

#mcq(18, [PAYE deducted from a worker's gross pay is],
  [an addition to gross pay],
  [a cost of the employer],
  [part of direct labour],
  [a liability to be paid to the tax authority]
)

#mcq(19, [The employer's own pension contribution is],
  [part of the cost of labour],
  [a loan to the worker],
  [a distribution of profit],
  [a deduction from the worker's pay]
)

#mcq(20, [The document used to record the time a worker spends on each job is the],
  [time book or job card],
  [payslip],
  [clock card],
  [stores requisition]
)

#mcq(21, [Budgeted overhead ₦500,000 over 25,000 labour hours. The absorption rate is],
  [₦20 per hour],
  [₦50 per hour],
  [₦25 per hour],
  [₦2 per hour]
)

#mcq(22, [Using the rate above, 24,000 hours were actually worked and the actual overhead was ₦470,000. Overhead was],
  [₦500,000 absorbed, ₦30,000 under-absorbed],
  [₦480,000 absorbed, ₦10,000 under-absorbed],
  [₦480,000 absorbed, ₦10,000 over-absorbed],
  [₦470,000 absorbed, ₦10,000 over-absorbed]
)

#mcq(23, [Under-absorption of overhead means that],
  [the budget was not prepared],
  [the overhead was all fixed],
  [the firm charged its products less than it spent],
  [the firm charged its products more than it spent]
)

#mcq(24, [Over-absorption is disposed of by],
  [crediting the profit and loss account],
  [debiting the profit and loss account],
  [carrying it to next year as stock],
  [adding it to capital]
)

#mcq(25, [Charging the whole rent of a building used only by the machine shop to that department is],
  [apportionment],
  [reapportionment],
  [allocation],
  [absorption]
)

#mcq(26, [Rent shared between departments on the basis of floor area is],
  [a direct expense],
  [absorption],
  [apportionment],
  [allocation]
)

#mcq(27, [The canteen cost of a factory is usually reapportioned on the basis of],
  [number of employees],
  [floor area],
  [machine hours],
  [capital employed]
)

#mcq(28, [Machine maintenance cost is reapportioned to production departments on the basis of],
  [floor area],
  [machine hours],
  [number of employees],
  [sales value]
)

#mcq(29, [Absorption of overhead into product cost is normally based on],
  [the number of products sold],
  [labour hours, machine hours or direct wages],
  [the value of closing stock],
  [the firm's profit]
)

#mcq(30, [The rate of stock turnover is computed as],
  [sales ÷ closing stock],
  [average stock ÷ cost of sales],
  [cost of sales ÷ average stock],
  [opening stock ÷ purchases]
)

#mcq(31, [A high rate of stock turnover generally indicates],
  [a stock loss],
  [efficient stock management],
  [overstocking],
  [slow-moving stock]
)

#mcq(32, [The cost of storing material, insurance of stock and interest on capital tied up in stock are],
  [stock-out costs],
  [ordering costs],
  [holding costs],
  [prime costs]
)

#mcq(33, [If a firm increases its order size, its total holding cost will],
  [stay the same],
  [rise],
  [become an ordering cost],
  [fall]
)

#mcq(34, [Labour turnover is measured as],
  [wages ÷ number of workers],
  [hours worked ÷ hours paid × 100],
  [the number of workers employed],
  [replacements ÷ average number employed × 100]
)

#mcq(35, [A high labour turnover is costly because of],
  [higher material prices],
  [higher stock values],
  [recruitment, training and lost production],
  [lower wages]
)

#mcq(36, [Gross pay less statutory and voluntary deductions gives],
  [take-home overtime],
  [the employer's cost],
  [basic pay],
  [net pay]
)

#mcq(37, [Employer's cost of labour is],
  [net pay],
  [gross pay plus the employer's own contributions],
  [gross pay less deductions],
  [basic pay only]
)

#mcq(38, [A stores item is received at ₦15 and later at ₦18. Under FIFO the closing stock, when prices are rising, is valued at],
  [an average of the two],
  [the newer price],
  [the older price],
  [the lower of the two]
)

#mcq(39, [The perpetual inventory system records stock],
  [once a month regardless of movements],
  [by physical count only],
  [continuously, at every receipt and issue],
  [only at the year end]
)

#mcq(40, [Which of these is a cost of holding stock rather than of ordering it?],
  [a telephone call to the supplier],
  [the clerk's time preparing an order],
  [the warehouse rent for the stock],
  [postage on a purchase order]
)

